From f5af7de7f8f44a1aa1b2de8d29ebdff1f34f5cca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 06:15:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Library entry section map: where a re-split entry's old pages
 and sentences are now
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Owner, 2026-11-15 (card: 'Keep page→section map'). A page-split entry
re-split by its headings renames its sections and their prose blocks, so
a citation made against the old split (library/<slug>/blocks/
prose-page-012, or an L1 coverage location p12:s3) named nothing.

- schemas/library/entry-section-map.ts: section-map.json
  (folio-library-section-map/v1), a derived file beside extraction.json,
  registered as a library node family with its validator, and declared
  as an entry sidecar for check:l1-complete.
- scripts/section-map.ts: buildSectionMap maps each old page-NNN to the
  new sections covering that PDF page (and their prose blocks), and each
  old pN:sM to the new (section, sentence) whose text is the same once
  normalised, or, marked 'part', holds it or is held by it (a running
  head before a page's first sentence, a sentence a page break cut).
  Nothing is placed by position; unmatched counts the rest. Sentences
  are split as folio-assistant-core's l1-coverage splits them (a copy:
  this layer may not import that one; core should import this).
  resolveCitation answers pN:sM, page-NNN, pN or an old prose-page block.
  A CLI builds the map from the filed entry or from a git ref, and
  resolves a citation.
- ingest --promote writes the map into the staged entry when the filed
  entry is a page split and the staged one is not.

On who-iris's two handbooks re-split by the pilot, read from the old
page files at 8d000b963^1: 409 of 464 and 749 of 872 old sentences
resolve (56 and 67 of them as part matches); every old page resolves to
its sections.

